          "message": "Add special webhook type for integration with git-pages (#14966)\n\nThe new webhook type is unusual compared to the existing one:\n * The git-pages webhook is only available for repositories. It makes\n   no sense to use this webhook for users, orgs, or globally.\n * The git-pages webhook has a fixed branch filter (`pages`) and event\n   list (`push_only`).\n * The git-pages webhook has a special behavior for \"Test delivery\"\n   button: it sends the last commit from the `pages` branch, not from\n   the default branch.\n\nThis should significantly reduce user frustration and Codeberg Pages\nsupport workload (while helping any other forge that uses git-pages\njust as much).\n\nPreview: https://codeberg.org/attachments/1408ca8f-2931-42a6-a903-0244ac44dca8\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14966\nReviewed-by: 0ko <redacted@example.invalid>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Ahlenstorf <redacted@example.invalid>\nReviewed-by: oliverpool <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
